From 542e5c8a4be27595af20693e396713dff4821aad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:31:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] options: stop the V-blank callback before freeing the app's
 buffers (SDK_PORT_3DS)

OptionsApp_Free frees the app's BgConfig and its other buffers in its first
call (setupAndFreeState 0) and stops Main_SetVBlankIntrCB only in its second
(setupAndFreeState 1), one frame later. The V-blank in between still runs
OptionsApp_OnVBlank, which calls DoScheduledBgGpuUpdates(data->bgConfig) on
the freed config. The NNS heap's free-list header has overwritten
bufferTransferScheduled and the bgs[] tilemap buffers, so a layer looks
scheduled and LoadBgVramScr starts a DMA from a scribbled pointer (0x02C002C0
in the PC run, count 0x2C0). The DS reads whatever the RAM holds and carries
on; the port's DMA dereferences that value as a host pointer and data-aborts,
which is the crash when the Settings menu is closed and the field is
returning.

Stop the callback with the buffers, as the app's siblings do. The #else text
is unchanged, so the Metrowerks build still preprocesses identically; the
only difference is that the one frame of garbage VRAM transfer the freed
config would have produced no longer happens.

Reproduced on the PC runner (new game -> bedroom -> mother -> X -> OPTIONS ->
QUIT): before this patch it aborts at the V-blank after the free, in
OptionsApp_OnVBlank -> DoScheduledBgGpuUpdates -> LoadBgVramScr; after it the
run returns to the field.
---
 src/options_app.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/options_app.c b/src/options_app.c
index 80c46cc..000efa1 100644
--- a/src/options_app.c
+++ b/src/options_app.c
@@ -516,6 +516,11 @@ static BOOL OptionsApp_Setup(OptionsApp_Data *data) {
 static BOOL OptionsApp_Free(OptionsApp_Data *data) {
     switch (data->setupAndFreeState) {
     case 0:
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+        // The port runs the V-blank between this call and case 1, while the
+        // app's callback is still installed, and it would update the freed bgConfig.
+        Main_SetVBlankIntrCB(NULL, NULL);
+#endif
         GF_DestroyVramTransferManager();
         OptionsApp_FreeWindows(data);
 
